    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0555" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/10798b:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-15T21:00:00-04:00">May 15, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>920. We suggest that you consult with Mallet with a view to calling on your
                    Soviet colleague,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d509-f1"/> if you have not already done
                    so, to inform her of the results of our negotiations to date with respect to
                    ball-bearing exports to the enemy in view of her Government’s support of our <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> to the Swedes in that connection.</p>
                <p>Sent to Stockholm, repeated to Moscow for information.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d509-f1" n="55" xml:id="d509-f1-content">
                <p>Mme. Alexandra Kollontay, Soviet Minister in Sweden.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
